00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.393
For this recipe,

00:05:47.393 --> 00:05:49.620
I'm just gonna have to
give it a 10 out of 10.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.500
So good.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.360
Let's move on to the next
one, the vegan unagi don.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.450
Our second recipe is this vegan unagi don,

00:05:55.450 --> 00:06:00.450
which is the eel made from eggplant.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.190
I actually have made something similar

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.240
with my friend Merle over on Goodful.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.290
It was absolutely delicious,

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.630
so I'm excited to try this recipe.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.810
This vegan unagi don recipe
is from Okonomi Kitchen.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.720
Let's watch the video.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.780
I mean, right off the bat,

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.970
it already straight up looks like eel.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.650
Okay, I got my rice going already.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.590
We're gonna steam our eggplant.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:23.580
So it looks like she
butterflied the eggplant,

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.460
spread it with her fingers.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.200
I'm really excited about this one.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.150
Let's get started.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.780
So first, to make the eel,

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.470
which is made out of eggplant today,

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.680
we're gonna need three Japanese eggplants,

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.100
or two Chinese eggplants.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.350
My eggplant today is extremely long,

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.320
and in this case, I would say size matters

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.880
and we'll only need one.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.620
So we're gonna remove the tip.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.260
I learned this tip from Merle.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.960
You don't need to just cut off the tip.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.260
We're wasting flesh here.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.230
You just take that little
leaf, peel it upwards.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.290
Minimize the food waste.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:56.910
And then now you only
need to cut this part off.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.080
I've definitely seen some videos

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.590
where people are cutting
off this much eggplant,

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.480
and it's all good stuff in there.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.130
I'm gonna cut this in half

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.620
and now we're just gonna
steam it for five minutes,

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.870
flipping it halfway through.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:11.850
All right, our eggplant
has finished steaming.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.440
Let's remove it.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.300
We're going to butterfly the eggplant.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.040
So we're gonna slice in
but not all the way through

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.930
and we are going to peel it outwards.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:25.160
Ooh, okay, this is working.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.290
No, this was great.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.450
Okay, perfect.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.453
Now she flattens it.

00:07:29.453 --> 00:07:32.070
Now we're gonna do the same
thing with this guy here.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:32.903
That looks great.

00:07:32.903 --> 00:07:33.920
I kinda cut through that one,

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.770
but let's just pretend I didn't.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.000
So now she creates little horizontal cuts.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.970
This looks so good.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:43.170
Our eggplant is ready,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.610
and now we are going to dust
it with some potato starch.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.120
Now we are going to pan fry them.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.820
I'm gonna do them one at a time.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.470
About two to three minutes on each side

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.580
until there's a little bit of a char,

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.130
and then we're gonna make
the sauce in the same pan.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.410
There's an option to make
the sauce on the side,

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.690
keep it real nice and neat,
but I'm a one pan kinda gal.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.810
Just keep it simple, do less dishes.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.200
Me and eggplant have come a very long way.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.780
I used to have such a
strong hatred towards it.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.260
I didn't like the flavor, the texture.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:15.030
But then I had the Chinese garlic eggplant

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.110
and now I love it in everything.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.206
I always say, if you don't like a food

00:08:19.206 --> 00:08:22.360
and it's been three years,
give it another try.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.420
Our flavor palettes are always expanding.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.260
All right, let's give this a flip.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.930
Right now, the eggplant
is sticking to the pot.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.900
If you just let it sit and crispify,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.520
you'll be able to move
in just a couple minutes,

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.420
so I always recommend just
leaving it once it's stuck.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.723
And let's repeat it with the second one,

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.020
and we're just gonna do the same thing

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.180
and then we'll make the sauce.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.770
To make the sauce, we're
gonna add some sake,

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.280
some mirin and dashi powder.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.890
So once that dashi is all dissolved,

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:53.680
gonna add in some cane
sugar and some soy sauce.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:58.000
I want this mixture to
thicken to about this texture,

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.380
and now we're gonna add
back in our eggplant,

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:04.610
get that beautifully
coated up in the sauce.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.560
And finally, we're just
gonna add nori, rice,

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.560
sauce, our eggplant

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:13.030
and finally, topped with
some toasted sesame seeds.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.550
This looks so good.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.690
Honestly, really looks a lot like eel.

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:17.793
Let's give this a try.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.670
That is so effing good!

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:23.800
If you're at home and you're
not gonna make any of these,

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:24.740
you gotta make this.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:28.590
The moisture and the juice
the eggplant gives off

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.770
is so complementary with the fluffy rice,

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.680
and also the eggplant has had that chance

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.243
to soak up all that sauce.

00:09:34.243 --> 00:09:36.110
It's in perfect harmony.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.040
10 out of 10.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.170
Let's move on to the next one,

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:39.770
salt and pepper flower mushrooms.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.500
So the next one we're moving on to

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.970
is the salt and pepper flower
mushrooms from Woon Heng.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:47.800
These look so cool.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.740
It reminds me of popcorn chicken kind of,

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:50.620
but with mushrooms,

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.130
and texture heaven with
all these crisscrosses.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.233
Let's watch the video.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.220
It looks so good.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.260
A flower for me?

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:00.093
Thank you.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.500
See, I just already can't wait to do that.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.100
It looks so fun, and then
coating it in the cornstarch.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.830
All the crispy bits, my gosh.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.710
Peppers all thrown together.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.310
If you've ever had a
dry pot, a dry hot pot,

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:16.903
it's dry seasonings, love, so good.

00:10:16.903 --> 00:10:17.736
It reminds me of chicken wings.

