is cut them into two
and a half inch slices.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:51.200
And last one.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.120
So now is that cool trick that she did.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.910
I've done this with potatoes once before

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:56.990
and it was really fun.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:57.900
Okay, so what we're gonna do

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.840
is line chopsticks on
either side of the mushroom,

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:02.770
like this.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:04.670
We're going to cut,

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:08.272
(mushroom squelching)

00:11:08.272 --> 00:11:09.510
until we hit the chopsticks,

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.430
so it doesn't go all the way through.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.350
All right, so now we
turn it around this way,

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:15.800
and same thing.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.580
I'm being really careful
not to cut any pieces off.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.520
Wow, look at that.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.896
Sorry if you have trypophobia,

00:11:21.896 --> 00:11:25.663
I can see if this'll trigger
you, but I think it looks cool.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.440
I'm just gonna finish cutting these

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.290
and then we'll move on to the next step.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.940
So I've cut all my mushrooms

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.550
and created my beautiful florets,

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:38.742
so I have, just kidding, it's not boiling.

00:11:38.742 --> 00:11:40.150
(Jasmine laughs)

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:42.480
We are going to place
our florets in there,

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.390
uncut side down.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.680
And then we're just gonna cook them

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.340
for about three to five minutes

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:50.940
until it turns from white
to a little grayish color.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.670
Ooh, they're blossoming!

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:53.670
How cute!

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.750
The mushrooms look slightly gray.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:57.730
I'm just gonna take them out

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.500
and we're gonna squeeze
out any excess moisture.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.480
I can already tell,

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.610
if I did it right now,
I'd burn my fingers,

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.000
which I do often 'cause I
don't have any patience.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.530
But anyway, this isn't about me.

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.660
I've let the mushrooms chill a little bit.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.510
Gently press on it to
remove that extra moisture.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:16.092
Because of all the little
crevices we made with the slicing,

00:12:16.092 --> 00:12:19.860
they're just gonna carry
a lot of extra moisture

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.150
and you wanna get that
out so it can be crispy.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.680
So now we're gonna add
our mushroom flowers

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.900
to our cornstarch mixture,

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:28.470
which just has some salt,
black pepper and white pepper,

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.850
and I just mixed it all together.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.960
Now we're gonna toss in the mushrooms.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.020
Just gonna get that all coated.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:37.590
Open it up, coat it in all the crevices.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.423
Look at that.

00:12:38.423 --> 00:12:40.060
Nice and coated.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:43.310
Gonna dust off any excess cornstarch

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.270
and then place it in our oil.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.440
Oh my gosh, beautiful.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:49.930
I don't wanna do too many at a time,

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.800
'cause I'm scared they're
gonna stick together.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:56.270
Okay, so we're gonna fry these
until they're golden brown.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:57.500
Are you a mushroom person?

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.630
Please let me know in the comments,

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.060
because when I was in third grade,

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.297
my teacher, she was like,

00:13:02.297 --> 00:13:03.817
"Okay, everyone's gonna come up here

00:13:03.817 --> 00:13:05.620
"and tell us your favorite food."

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.657
I went up and said mushrooms
and the whole class said, "Ew!"

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.730
But I remember that moment so clearly.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.040
(Jasmine laughs)

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.800
These look great.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.600
Gonna add some more.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.380
Don't touch each other.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.180
I'm like an RA at college.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:21.690
Okay, these look done.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.080
Look how pretty it is.

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.190
It literally looks like a flower.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.650
Put it on my paper lined plate here

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:30.340
to drain that extra oil.

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:33.150
We're gonna make the dry
rub, the dry seasonings.

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:36.230
I'm gonna add some oil to my pan here.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:39.180
Oil's hot, let's toss in
the garlic, red chile,

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:43.810
scallions, salt, white
pepper and some black pepper.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.670
The colors are so vibrant.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:49.393
Let's toss in our mushrooms
that we just fried.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:58.100
So the best method is to toss it gently.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.700
Okay, this is all done.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.590
So last step is to just drizzle
some sesame oil over it.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.020
Don't overdo it.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.840
If I was having movie
night with my friends

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.610
and we were eating dinner and stuff,

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.344
this would be the perfect appetizer

00:14:11.344 --> 00:14:13.950
or side dish of the meal.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.320
The mushrooms are finally done.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.900
They look beautiful.

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:18.970
I mean, they do straight
up look like flowers,

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.310
which is very very impressive to me.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:22.313
Let's get to eating.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.010
You hear the crunch?

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.350
Just reminds me of popcorn chicken.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.950
There's a lot of peppers in here.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:31.460
It's not actually too spicy.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.280
It's definitely more of a peppery kick.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:36.060
The scallions and the sesame
help neutralize everything

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.130
and the crisp of the mushroom, oh my gosh.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.460
It tastes like chicken.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:43.580
Honestly, there's nothing I
would do to change this dish.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.720
It is perfect as is.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.050
The bubble potato pillows

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.630
were deliciously crispy on the outside,

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.080
creamy in the center.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:55.150
The vegan unagi don, oh
my gosh, the eggplant!

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:59.220
The juice from it, it was so so good.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:03.400
Paired with the rice and he
sauce, it was just chef's kiss.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:06.200
And of course, the salt and
pepper flower mushrooms.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.600
Crispy, peppery, nutty.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:09.940
So so good.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.610
All right guys, thanks
so much for watching.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:14.550
All these dishes were so good,
10 out of 10 for all of them.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:15.900
If you plan on making any of them,

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.300
the links are in the description.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:20.090
Snap a picture, tag me on
Instagram 'cause I wanna see.

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:22.130
Bye guys!

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.713
(upbeat music)

